    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2e1669a692e00554c969caeec97544ae7cbdcddb4d8a13d4605dcdb522532dcf",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The failure of tested level perturbations and prime-level deletion locates the missing oscillations outside those changes to one-particle levels and motivates promoting the scalar pairing coupling to a level-dependent matrix. Requiring the antisymmetric time-reversal-breaking term to retain its simple form under elimination selects, within the paper's ansatz, max-index and min-index coupling patterns with opposite RG directions. In the continuum, their integrated-amplitude and gauge transformations produce Schrödinger problems with potentials V_+=one half dg_D/dq and V_-=-one half dg_D/dq, making coupling gradients—not constant coupling offsets—candidate carriers of a scattering phase for the oscillatory count.",
